<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.claude.accounts-local — STAGED, NOT LOADED. The 20 s local refresh for the account board and
  the router: auth state and live sessions, read from this machine only, with no call to the usage
  endpoint (docs/plans/ACCOUNTS_BOARD_FRESHNESS.md D9).

  WHY IT LIVES IN launchd/staged/ AND NOT launchd/. A plist in launchd/ is COPIED to
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents by install.sh and macOS arms it at the next login. launchd/staged/ is
  outside install.sh's non-recursive glob, so this job starts only when the operator runs
  migration 0063 (tests/install-staged-plist.bats).

  THE `ts` CONTRACT. `claude-accounts --local-refresh` never writes the cache's `ts`. `ts` is the
  age of the last USAGE sweep, and keepwarm's `--max-age 90` reads it to decide whether to sweep.
  A local pass every 20 s that moved `ts` would make the cache look forever fresh and silence every
  keepwarm sweep, so the usage figures would stop moving while the board looked current. The local
  pass writes its own overlay and touches its own stamp, nothing else.

  FLOOR PLUS ACCELERATOR. StartInterval 20 is the guarantee: the board's auth and session columns
  are never more than ~20 s plus one pass behind. WatchPaths on login.keychain-db is only an
  accelerator, so a /login shows up in seconds rather than at the next tick. It cannot be the
  guarantee: `man launchd.plist` calls WatchPaths race-prone (an event between two loads is lost),
  and FSEvents went dark on this machine on 2026-09-08, during which no WatchPaths job fired at all.
  ThrottleInterval 10 stops a burst of keychain writes from relaunching it back to back.

  ProcessType Interactive (since 2026-10-20; was Standard), with no LowPriorityIO: keepwarm's
  2026-09-24 note records a PRI-4 tick that sat 3h40m in dyld under load. A local pass is well under
  a second of CPU, so the clamp buys nothing and costs freshness. Standard was meant to give PRI 31
  and gave 20 (`ps -M` read 20T, G2 review R6): the utility band, where rail work ran 7-111x slower
  at load ~200. This job writes the router's auth and session overlay, so its band is the router's.
  Reload with `bash ~/.claude/scripts/limit-recover/lr-band-reload.sh --keepwarm`, then
  `--confirm keepwarm-band` (operator batch RK).

  A DEADLINE THAT COVERS STARTUP. `perl -e 'alarm N; exec ...'` arms the kernel timer before the
  exec, and a pending alarm survives execve, so a stall in exec, dyld or imports ends with exit 142
  at 120 s instead of holding the job (launchd never overlaps ticks).

  KILL SWITCHES, in ~/.claude/state/accounts-local/ (CC_ACCOUNTS_LOCAL_DIR overrides):
    off              the pass prints `local: disabled`, touches the stamp, and does nothing else
                     (the env form is CC_ACCOUNTS_LOCAL=off)
    first-read-off   turns off the first-read path (bin/claude-accounts documents it)
    census-ps        the live-session census uses ps instead of the native libproc census
  The stamp, ~/.claude/logs/accounts-local.stamp, is the liveness evidence (fleet.manifest).

  Install: bash ~/Development/claude-infrastructure/migrations/0063-accounts-local-job.sh --confirm launchd
  Uninstall: launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.claude.accounts-local; rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.claude.accounts-local.plist
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.claude.accounts-local</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>-c</string>
    <string>export PATH="$HOME/.claude/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin"; exec /usr/bin/perl -e 'alarm shift; exec @ARGV or die "exec: $!"' 120 "$HOME/.claude/bin/claude-accounts" --local-refresh</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>20</integer>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <key>WatchPaths</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/chrisren/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db</string>
  </array>

  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>10</integer>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Interactive</string>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/accounts-local.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/accounts-local.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
